#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:114
msgid "Typical sharing configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:116
msgid ""
"There are a few common ways to architect sharing, with trade-offs between"
" them, and you should choose the one that best fits your use case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:121
msgid "Bulk passwords"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:123
msgid ""
"If you want to limit access to a group of users, you can create a "
"password for each user, and then share the password with them. This "
"allows users to access the documentation directly, but requires more "
"management on your end. Any time a new user needs access or you want to "
"remove access, you will need to generate a new password for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:132
msgid "Authenticated redirect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:134
msgid ""
"If you want to share documentation with a group of users, you need to "
"authenticate those users against your own system first. The simplest way "
"to do this is to create an authenticated redirect on your site, which "
"then redirects to the Read the Docs :ref:`commercial/sharing:secret "
"link`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:139
msgid ""
"This should require minimal customization, and will ensure that only "
"authenticated users can access the documentation. The downside is that "
"users won't be able to access the documentation directly from a bookmark,"
" and will have to go through your site first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:145
msgid "Authenticated proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:147
msgid ""
"If you want a more transparent experience for your users, you can create "
"a proxy that authenticates users against your system, and then proxies "
"the request to Read the Docs. This is more complex to set up, but will "
"allow users to access the documentation directly from a bookmark."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/commercial/sharing.rst:153
msgid ""
"This approach would use a :ref:`commercial/sharing:HTTP Authorization "
"Header` to authenticate users, and would be configured in your proxy "
"server."
msgstr ""

